] [17592186420150 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b05ca4a9-4343-56a3-86ae-980793c8602f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420151 #edb/ref 1080 "r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420151 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420151 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f59eba3d-6e2f-504f-905a-a227d63c2c42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420152 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420152 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420152 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420152 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420152 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420152 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420152 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420152 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420152 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f9a0d8dd-871f-5fc8-9699-7a78c5f80aac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420153 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420153 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127921" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420153 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420153 #edb/ref 1071 "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨5,-1,3⟩=27.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420153 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3fa29ff6-5ae4-5642-82fd-03b1645e810c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420153 #edb/ref 1074 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨5,-1,3⟩=27$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨5,-1,3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨5,-1,3⟩ & =0 \\\\ 5{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =5{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,5{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420154 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420154 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6262b847-bfad-5541-b7d9-0c48d99eb024" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420154 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186393043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420155 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420155 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f1edd60-137c-5af0-bf08-f3f3e9df0344" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420155 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186262846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420156 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420156 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7c175861-cf16-5bce-9a3d-7dd7700bfeb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420156 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420157 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420157 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8d1b2442-6684-5f23-a6d5-881beb105644" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420157 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186120224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420158 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f1fe54dc-0b25-528c-81fb-caa7a89e418f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420158 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186262859 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
